{"skill":{"slug":"conventional-commits","displayName":"Conventional Commits"},"version":{"version":"1.0.1","createdAt":1769695599193,"changelog":"- Added metadata section with author and version information to the skill definition.\n- No changes to functionality or documentation content.","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4990,"sha256":"19f603530737f7f6077ff4e0a0f3e87c899ed910d73ab83f9daefb3ba87cb33d","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1606,"sha256":"dff248654ae6c70c01ae841548ba6c0f2e3fbe28d1ea8ff1b9fd836570a6bf10","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789015709265,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"1830fe9496786f489ab1ad12dd6804fdd5d48d028ee1293b18d29fa0617ac207","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/1830fe9496786f489ab1ad12dd6804fdd5d48d028ee1293b18d29fa0617ac207","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: conventional-commits\nVersion: 1.0.1\n\nThe skill bundle is benign. It consists of a standard metadata file and a markdown document (`SKILL.md`) that solely provides instructions and examples for formatting commit messages according to the Conventional Commits specification. There is no executable code, no external network calls, no file system access, and no evidence of prompt injection attempts designed to manipulate the agent into performing malicious actions, data exfiltration, or unauthorized operations. The content is purely informational and aligns with its stated purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779159763068},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":8,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":2,"checkedAt":1789015709265},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a Markdown-only guide for formatting commit messages and shows no evidence of code execution, data access, persistence, or hidden behavior.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill does not request file, network, credential, tool, or system access; its instructions are proportionate to commit-message formatting assistance.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The inspected package contains only artifact/SKILL.md; no scripts, dependencies, install hooks, or executable components were present in the artifact evidence.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The trigger and wording are broad enough to apply Conventional Commit formatting whenever commits are discussed, which may be stylistically over-eager, but it does not create a security-impacting authority or hidden behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No persistence, privilege escalation, background execution, memory-writing behavior, or tool modification was found.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact's purpose is to help format commit messages using Conventional Commits, and its content is limited to syntax, examples, and writing guidelines.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this if you want agents to prefer Conventional Commit formatting. Be aware it may nudge commit-message discussions toward that format even when a repository does not require it.","findings":"[SQP-1] expected: The broad activation language is real but limited to when commit-related help is being discussed; it is a usability/scope note rather than a security concern.\n[SQP-3] expected: The universal formatting instruction matches the skill's stated style-guide purpose, though users should ensure it fits their repository conventions.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789015709265}}}}}